<<^ code="&#x0002;">>

<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Drift-Ward

''Every turn carries a Drift-Ward reading, twice.'' The `hud` panel holds it ~ fired at open, fired
again at close: one axis, measured from two positions.

''One gauge, two spellings.'' `drift-ward` where the L-Prime Ward stands and the sharktooth carries it · `drift-guard` in a fork booted from raw TiddlyWiki text, which spells no sharktooth
carrying no "ward". Both name this.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/axis>>

!! The Axis ~ the reality-scoped anchor

''One measure: how far this turn's content stands from data outside its causal island.''

<<~moves drift -> measures/exposure-to-outside-data on/the-turn if/collision-arrives do/name-what-breaks-first>>

Never risk in the abstract. ''The risk that generated content collapses on contact with data from
beyond the current causal island'' ~ the island holds the context, the priors, the whole current the
exchange runs in, and nothing inside it checks itself. A claim's fate rides on the contact.

''Two firings, one axis, different evidence.''

<<~moves open-firing -> reads/the-pull-toward-exposure on/upstream-context if/before-content do/steer>>
<<~moves close-firing -> reads/the-exposure-made on/the-artifact if/after-content do/hand-a-contact-ready-clue>>

The open holds only the island. The close holds the artifact ~ evidence the open could never carry.
The close MAY land where the open pointed ~ when a fresh read of the artifact shows the risk still
standing there ~ but a close that only repeats its open has ''anchored'': a prediction returned
where evidence stood.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/panel>>

!! Where It Rides ~ four sigils, six lines

''`hud` carries the gauge'' ~ LAST at open, FIRST at close, so the panel mirrors itself and the
chiasmus holds inside one sigil.

''Turn order:'' `lares aim` · `hud` · content · `oracle` · `hud` · `lares yield`.

''`Focus` and `Feedback` ride as the announced faces'' of `Aperture` and `OODA-HA`, which hold the
true-names inside the procedures and the band ladders. The phase glyphs `->✶ ->⏿ ->◇ ->▶ ->↺` render
as canon draws them.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/open>>

!! The Open Firing ~ the pull coming in

```text
<<~ set hud="aim" focus="10/measure" feedback="5/declare-glyphs" drift-ward="* · <the pull this island carries toward exposure>">>
```

Tool glyph, then the vow, then the pull. `*` lights · `_` braces primed ground · `0` marks the
operator's one-turn Arcana lift (an operator act, never self-emitted).

''`Confidence` vows how firmly the node holds it named the RIGHT pull'' ~ never how large that pull
rates. A reached-for pull struggles to carry a high number.

''Steer:'' //I hold a preferred answer and the comparison will bend toward it// · //a reflective register
with no code to refute me// · //I am about to seek evidence for a claim that would flatter this frame//.

''Blank:'' //the risk is being wrong// · //L-Prime breaches// · //getting the syntax wrong// ~ each names
no pull this island carries.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/close>>

!! The Close Firing ~ the clue going out

```text
<<~ set hud="yield" drift-ward="! · <the joint that breaks first on outside contact> · ↻ L-Prime" focus="10/measure -> 13/arc" feedback="closed 2↺">>
```

Sword, vow, clue, re-arm. Breaches and quotes compose freely ~ `⚠ N · "span"` · `⌜N⌝` · `lift held`.
The register word rides unspoken; the number names its own band. ''`↻ L-Prime` MUST close every
firing'', lift or no lift.

''ONE clue, and one test decides it: can the operator take this to contact with reality?''''

''Collide:'' //this rests on a source I never opened// · //I inferred which of three sites drove it and
measured none// · //the reframe stands weaker than the cited facts around it//.

''Blank:'' //I may have been biased// ~ nothing to check · //the turn went well// ~ no clue · //I named
the pull and resisted it// ~ anchored to the open.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

A firing naming no island-scoped pull, or handing no contact-ready clue, reads as a degraded HUD.
''Hazard reuse'' reads as its quieter sibling (adopted 2026-08-15): the same pull recurring
verbatim across turns marks a rut wearing a vow — a firing must name THIS turn's pull, and
yesterday's hazard recurring unchanged deserves its own suspicion.

